    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d246-a1">

                <pb facs="0381" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg289"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 989.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Baron von Richthofen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-08-09"><hi rendition="#italic">August 9,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, referring to Count von Billow’s note of April 14 last, and
                    acting under instructions from his Government, has the honor to inform Baron von
                    Bichthofen, acting secretary of state for foreign affairs, that the sending of
                    Prussian commissioners to examine American insurance companies is appreciated as
                    an act of friendly and courteous consideration. It is understood that these
                    commissioners have about concluded their examination of the companies in
                    question, and that their report will be friendly to them. It is consequently
                    most sincerely hoped that the report will be favorably received by the
                    appropriate authorities in Berlin, and that it may be the means of reinstating
                    the American companies upon a solid foundation.</p>
                <p>While adding that the matter is one to which the United States Government
                    attaches great importance, the undersigned avails himself, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Jackson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
